A||||5||Hartz||Alternative aero trim attachment ideas?||||1||
Z||000000||Hartz||10-30-2001||04:33 PM||||I am converting my '84 to an aero coupe, and am looking for a short cut to install the ground effects.  The tabs and slots are OK, but I'd like to avoid drilling holes and messing with fussy plastic clips.  The top of the ground effects seems flat enough.  Has anybody ever use some of that 3M double-sized automotive tape?  What about a nice bead of clear silcone?  <P>Any thoughts appreciated.<P>Thanks,<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||10-30-2001||04:50 PM||||I don't see any reason this method wouldn't work.  I've been thinking about it too because I don't want to drill holes in the doors etc.<P>First place I'd check an automotive paint store, they might have some thin trim tape that would hold up.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-30-2001||05:03 PM||||the 3M tape works fine. Make sure where you put it sets flush though, it wont hold in a gap. clean it with alcohol. warm the panels with a hair dryer to help it stick. dont get it wet for a day or two. make sure you have it positioned right, because it sticks hard immediatly on contact.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-30-2001||06:20 PM||||You could easily use some good old duct tape to stick the new front fascia on.  Just like the race cars.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000004||Hartz||10-30-2001||06:24 PM||||Careful there Old Lar - you're hitting a little too close to home!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> <P>With Red Duct Tape:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front_sm.jpg">  <P>I like to call it my Talladega aero package.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(Yes, I have a new hood and will be putting it on soon...)<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com<p>[This message has been edited by Hartz (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||11-02-2001||05:17 PM||||Thanks again to those who replied.  That 3M tape appears to work quite well.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/moulding.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt_side.JPG"> <P>Now to decide on some paint...<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
